---
title: "Centralized Logging Platform"
category: "Observability & Reliability"
difficulty: "Hard"
tags: ["logging", "search", "data-pipelines", "security", "multi-tenancy", "pii"]
---

## Overview

This platform ingests logs at high volume from many producers, enforces centrally managed PII redaction before data becomes searchable, and provides fast search plus near-real-time tailing for incident response. It uses a durable ingestion buffer to absorb spikes, a deterministic processing step as the policy boundary, and two storage tiers: a hot search index for interactive queries and low-cost object storage for long retention and forensics.

---

## Requirements

### Functional
- Ingest via HTTP and gRPC, including OpenTelemetry Logs; accept JSON and text.
- Multi-tenancy with authN/authZ, quotas, per-tenant retention, and isolation.
- Centrally managed PII policies applied before data is searchable by default.
- Schema evolution (new fields, type changes, parser updates) without downtime or data loss.
